{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0131oEpGC7ccHGSU72cQs9Ly","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** GNU coreutils have no formal specifications accessible to implementers. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via an AI pipeline, and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** A four-stage pipeline (extract, specify, synthesize, verify) with `cmd/` per-utility packages, `pkg/` shared libraries (sys, format, testutils, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil), and `docs/specs/` holding SRDs as the source of truth. mage-claude-orchestrator drives code generation.\n\n**Current state:** 114 SRDs specified, ~70 utilities implemented across 33 releases. This is generation-run44. Recent commits show work on cmd/dir (srd107 R1.5, R2.1-R2.3 just completed).\n\n**Current release focus:** Release 13.0 is the earliest release with `ready` requirements in `requirement_states`: srd106-df (10 reqs), srd107-dir (1 req: R2.4), srd108-vdir (10 reqs), srd109-dircolors (14 reqs).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 13.0 has four utilities with ready requirements. srd107-dir needs only R2.4 to complete (cmd/dir already has code from task 5608). srd108-vdir is entirely unimplemented (all 10 requirements ready). Completing dir first provides a reference for vdir (both are ls wrappers). With a 4-task limit and impl/test split required, I allocate 2 tasks to finish dir and 2 tasks to start vdir implementation.\n\n## Weight Budget Verification\n\n```\nTask 0: srd107-dir R2.4 (w=1) → total=1 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 1: srd107-dir R2.4 (w=1, test) → total=1 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 2: srd108-vdir R1.1(1) + R1.2(1) + R1.3(1) + R1.4(1) → total=4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 3: srd108-vdir R1.5(1) + R1.6(1) + R2.1(1) + R2.2(1) → total=4 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\n(Weights assumed default=1; actual weights from requirements.yaml not available in project_context.)\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/dir: implement srd107 R2.4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd107-dir.yaml (R2.4 requirement details)\n      - cmd/dir/main.go (existing implementation -- R1.1-R1.5, R2.1-R2.3 already implemented)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/dir/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add R2.4 functionality to existing dir implementation\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd107 R2.4 as specified in the SRD, extending the existing cmd/dir implementation\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Extend the existing cmd/dir/main.go -- do not rewrite or restructure code for R1.1-R1.5, R2.1-R2.3\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Preserve the existing sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() call at the start of main\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"dir is equivalent to ls -C -b -- maintain this equivalence when adding R2.4\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/dir/main.go compiles with go build -o bin/dir ./cmd/dir/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"R2.4 behavior matches the SRD specification\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Existing functionality for R1.1-R1.5, R2.1-R2.3 is preserved unchanged\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/dir/ reports no issues\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/dir: test srd107 R2.4\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd107-dir.yaml (R2.4 requirement and acceptance criteria)\n      - cmd/dir/main.go (implementation to test)\n      - cmd/dir/dir_test.go (existing tests to extend)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests API)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/dir/dir_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases for R2.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Add differential test cases to cmd/dir/dir_test.go that verify srd107 R2.4 behavior against the gdir reference binary\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use testutils.RunDiffTests with testutils.BuildBinary(t, \\\".\\\") for the Go binary and exec.LookPath(\\\"gdir\\\") for the reference binary\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Call t.Skip if the gdir reference binary is not found in PATH\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Add test cases to the existing []testutils.DiffTest slice -- do not create a separate test function\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/dir/ -count=1 passes (or skips if gdir not installed)\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"New test cases exercise the R2.4 behavior specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Existing test cases for R1.1-R1.5, R2.1-R2.3 are preserved unchanged\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Tests set LC_ALL=C in the environment\"\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/vdir: implement srd108 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd108-vdir.yaml (R1.1-R1.4 requirement details)\n      - cmd/dir/main.go (reference implementation for a similar ls-wrapper utility)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (SIGPIPE handler API)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/vdir/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: Initial vdir implementation covering R1.1-R1.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd108 R1.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd108 R1.2 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd108 R1.3 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd108 R1.4 as specified in the SRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"vdir is